# Build context exclusions for backend/Dockerfile.
#
# It lives here and not at the repository root because the build context is `backend/`
# — the image needs nothing from `frontend/` or `docs/` — and because a config file
# that affects one package belongs inside that package (CLAUDE.md §2.3). Docker reads
# `.dockerignore` from the context root, so this is both the correct place and the only
# place it works from.
#
# The first entries are not about size. A `.env` inside the build context can be copied
# into a layer by a careless `COPY`, and a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the
# image. CLAUDE.md §3.3 forbids committing those files; this forbids shipping them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never in an image layer
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.crt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not part of the runtime
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The test suite does not ship: it never runs inside the image, and it carries
# fixtures and fakes that have no business in a runtime container.
tests
docker-compose.yml

# Python local artefacts
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
*.egg-info
